        <description>
            The Regolith Adherence Characterization (RAC) experiment photographs a number of sample materials 
            over time as they are exposed to the Lunar environment, in order to characterize regolith changes 
            on the samples. Wheel A is exposed from launch through landing, while Wheel B is covered until 
            after landing.  This camera covers the top side of wheel B.  Note that on TO-19D, wheel B 
            failed before launch and was not used.
        </description>
